010U75wdxE","it":"razzo-lanciato-di-notte-m010U75wdxE","ko":"야간에-발사된-로켓-m010U75wdxE","de":"rakete-in-der-nacht-gestartet-m010U75wdxE","pt":"foguete-lancado-a-noite-m010U75wdxE","id":"roket-diluncurkan-pada-malam-hari-m010U75wdxE"},"created_at":"2018-07-01T12:34:42Z","updated_at":"2026-02-18T00:21:27Z","promoted_at":"2018-07-01T13:42:02Z","width":2932,"height":3665,"color":"#0c2659","blur_hash":"LI8qW}roD%OZ4mOaofxFxmsm%2Rk","description":"The June 29, 2018 launch of a SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket from Cape Canaveral Air Force Station was scheduled for 5:42:42 AM in order to rendezvous with the International Space Station. Every rocket has a plume of exhaust, but only the rockets launching just before sunrise will show up like this one. Once the rocket reaches a certain altitude, the Sun below the horizon will light up the exhaust. (It is the same effect that causes noctilucent clouds). \r\nThis photo is a composite of a 235-second streak shot at f/22 and then a 4-second shot of the plume. This plume was visible across Florida.","alt_description":"rocket launched at nighttime","breadcrumbs":[],"urls":{"raw":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1530447920184-b88c8872?ixlib=rb-4.1.0","full":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1530447920184-b88c8872?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=85&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=srgb","regular":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1530447920184-b88c8872?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&w=1080&fit=max","small":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1530447920184-b88c8872?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&w=400&fit=max","thumb":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1530447920184-b88c8872?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&q=80&fm=jpg&crop=entropy&cs=tinysrgb&w=200&fit=max","small_s3":"https://s3.us-west-2.amazonaws.com/images.unsplash.com/small/photo-1530447920184-b88c8872"},"links":{"self":"https://api.unsplash.com/photos/rocket-launched-at-nighttime-m010U75wdxE","html":"https://unsplash.com/photos/rocket-launched-at-nighttime-m010U75wdxE","download":"https:/